# vkIFrames settings (live.conf). install.sh created this file because there was none; it will not touch it again.
#
# Every line below is a comment, so this file changes nothing until you remove the "# " in front of a line. A line that is active here OVERRIDES the same
# setting in the game's launch options (for example VKIFRAME_TARGET_FPS=90): uncomment only what you want to set from here.
#
# * Settings in the first group are picked up within a second while a game runs: just save the file.
# * Settings in the second group are read once when a game starts: change them, then restart the game.
# * The Decky panel (Steam Deck) rewrites this whole file when it starts and when you change a setting there: edits made by hand are overwritten then.
# * Write plain names (TARGET_FPS=90). A value that is not a number (or on/off) is ignored and noted in live.log. The values shown are the built-in defaults.
# * More about every setting: the README, and the layer's log ~/.config/vkiframes/live.log.

# --- changes apply while the game runs ---
# ENABLED=1                (1 = the layer works, 0 = games run as if it were not there; 0 or 1)
# TARGET_FPS=60            (the frame rate to reach; 30 to 120; the built-in default is 90 on a Steam Deck OLED)
# MAX_SYNTHETIC=3          (most generated frames between two game frames; 1 to 4)
# BASE_FPS_CAP=45          (limit the game's own frame rate to this; 0 = no limit; 0 to 90; choose Target FPS divided by a whole number)
# MIN_GAIN=1.01            (generate only when the target is at least this much above the game's rate; 1.01 to 1.5)
# PHASE_LOCK=1             (align generated frames with the game's frames when the ratio is close to a whole number; 0 or 1)
# PHASE_OFFSET=0.5         (where generated frames sit between two game frames; 0 to 0.999)
# INTERP_BIDIR=1           (two-sided optical flow; only with OPTICAL_FLOW=1; 0 or 1)
# CMD_BUFFERS=8            (how far the layer may queue ahead of the GPU; 4 to 32)
# SYNTH_MARGIN=0.15        (keeps generated frames this far from the game's frames; 0 to 0.45)

# --- read once when a game starts: change, then restart the game ---
# OPTICAL_FLOW=0           (1 = move the in-between frames along the motion; 0 = plain cross-fade; needs a game restart; 0 or 1)
# EXTRAPOLATE=0            (1 = low-latency mode, predicts instead of holding a frame; needs a game restart; 0 or 1)
# UI_MASK_THRESHOLD=0.08   (keeps still parts such as the HUD from being dragged; 0 = off; needs a game restart; 0 to 0.2)
# FLOW_LEVEL=2             (how finely motion is detected, 1 = finest; needs a game restart; 1 to 3)
